e-workers/linear/14069769/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d072232f3ad8a49ff32334e626619bf744c2b93b2dacf8a0d6a3562c3a3f5c1" "basis" 2418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-83710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=3,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ and\n\n- the $3$rd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{3}=3.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d072232f3ad8a49ff32334e626619bf744c2b93b2dacf8a0d6a3562c3a3f5c1" "basis" 2418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-83710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fba20b775935b352073a60c9f679b7174472b2490f4ea3737700991b80c2658" "basis" 2418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-83710" "field" "select