ation.json"} {"question" "q-140135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d072232f3ad8a49ff32334e626619bf744c2b93b2dacf8a0d6a3562c3a3f5c1" "basis" 2418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d072232f3ad8a49ff32334e626619bf744c2b93b2dacf8a0d6a3562c3a3f5c1" "basis" 2418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d072232f3ad8a49ff32334e626619bf744c2b93b2dacf8a0d6a3562c3a3f5c1" "basis" 2418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d072232f3ad8a49ff32334e626619bf744c2b93b2dacf8a0d6a3562c3a3f5c1" "basis" 2418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-84592" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A$ for which ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=3,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=0$ are eigenvalues, and\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nare the respective eigenvectors. What are the values of $a,b,c$ given that\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ a & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ a & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & b\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d072232f3ad8a49ff32334e626619bf744c2b93b2dacf8a0d6a3562c3a3f5c1" "basis" 2418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-84592" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=3,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=0,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal: \n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4,$\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=3,$ and\n\n- the $3$rd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{3}=0.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 13\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 13\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 13\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, we get $a=2,$ $b=13,$ and $c=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d072232f3ad8a49ff32334e626619bf744c2b93b2dacf8a0d6a3562c3a3f5c1" "basis" 2418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-84592" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fba20b775935b352073a60c9f679b7174472b2490f4ea3737700991b80c2658" "basis" 2418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-84592" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d072232f3ad8a49ff32334e626619bf744c